==============================================================
  CLMSynth -- User-Friendly Configuration Generator
==============================================================

  What this does: your data already has CLUSTERS. This tool adds a SECOND
  label on top and lets you dial how strongly it agrees with those clusters
  -- from an exact copy (score MCC = 1.0) down to no relationship (MCC ~ 0).
  You choose how many labels, how big each is, and where they sit.

  Press Enter to accept the [default] shown in brackets.

==============================================================
1. Data source -- where the clusters come from
==============================================================

Choose where the base clusters come from:
  clustbench : real benchmark datasets downloaded online (Gagolewski suite)
  mdcgen     : synthetic clusters generated on the fly (needs the mdcgenpy package)
  dummy      : tiny offline example data (no internet, no extra packages)
  byoc       : your OWN CSV file (features + one cluster-id column)
    1) clustbench
    2) mdcgen
    3) dummy
    4) byoc
  Data source [clustbench]: 
Where results go. Usually just press Enter to keep 'OUTPUT';
each run still gets its own timestamped subfolder inside it.
(Pick a plain folder name -- not the same name as a file.)
  Where to save results (folder) [OUTPUT]: 
